"""Human part 82b: the meleeTracker actor's controller choice, save / load, mission life cycle and frame setup
(game/melee_tracker.cpp: SetController, SaveGame, LoadGame and its leaf helper, the destructor, CopyFrom, StartMission,
the head overrides' and the sightings' release, StopMission, RestartMission, ReloadModel, SetupFrame, SetFrame,
WriteProperties, ReadProperties), against the original's.

Run: melee_tracker/build_mt.bat, MUT_WRAPPER=mt_diff.cpp, HD2_MT_QUICK=1 (20,000 sensing scenarios and 8,000 life
scenarios, about 14 s); the link options -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000 -Wl,--wrap=_ZN24C_MeleeTrackerController7DisableEv
-lwinmm. Lines 191-225, 533-769, 799-828, 834-1016, 1085-1115. Labels: G + the line.

Result (2026-11-22): 439 mutants, 40 not building; 361 of the 399 building killed (345 in the first run; the rest after
the harness fixes below), 38 survived, all equivalent or out of the comparison's reach:
- Equivalent: array sizes (G 548, 659 the quaternion's, 947 the bone name's); ReadProperties' version, read and never
  used (G 1108); SetupFrame's look-state stores that its SetLookBehaviour call writes again or tests against a state it
  never is (G 961, 968, 969 del / num / code, 970 del / num / code, 971 del / num / code).
- The controller replaced or released (SetController, StopMission, RestartMission: G 219, 220, 877, 878, 914, 915): the
  old one is freed, its Detach's write and its delete unobservable after (a leak at most).
- The destructor's stores and frees (G 804 code, 806 del / code, 807, 810 del / code, 811, 814 del / code, 815): the
  block is not compared after it (g++ drops a destructor's dead stores; a swapped free frees another list's array, which
  the test never reads again).
- ReleaseSightings' loop (G 863 the last entry kept, 864 none released): the sightings go back to each side's own pool,
  not compared.
- Out of the tests' reach: a closed chunk (G 537: SaveGame is always given an open one); a null entry in the seen list
  (G 593, 717: OnSightEvent never pushes one, so -1 is never saved or loaded); ReadIntLeaf's local (G 626: the cuts
  stay out of the id leaves, where the original reads a stack word); the timer leaf's local (G 661: a cut right after
  that leaf's header, not drawn in the quick run).

Harness fixes the first run showed (my mistakes): the save files were logged through Log's 600-byte buffer, so a save
was compared only up to its first ~290 bytes (the sightings' and the seen list's leaves never: G 580, 583); the chunk
depth was not logged, so a missing Ascend that Close made good went unseen (G 605, 606, 609, 743); the tracker's m_538
was always 0 before SetupFrame (G 973); the sight id 0 was rare (G 756 cmp / num); the load's cuts fell at ten fixed
steps only, never right after a leaf's header (G 658, 660); no file ended after the top chunk's header (G 646).
"""
